{
  "_note": "THE FIT AND ALIGNMENT FOLD — the artboard-into-box placement, and the one piece of geometry in this corpus. THE LAW. (1) Six fit words (cover · contain · fill · fitWidth · fitHeight · none) and nine alignment positions, both folded case-insensitively and with separators stripped, so `Bottom-Right`, `bottomright` and `bottomRight` are one word. `top`/`bottom`/`left`/`right` are the aliases of the four edge centres. (2) An unknown word FOLDS TO THE DEFAULT and is DIAGNOSED rather than refused: a typo in a presentation attribute must not blank an animation, but it must not be silent either. An ABSENT attribute is not a diagnostic. (3) Scale is exact and shared: contain = min, cover = max, fill = per-axis, fitWidth/fitHeight = one axis, none = 1. Placement is align * (box - content * scale), so the same nine factors serve every fit. (4) A zero-sized artboard is diagnosed and placed at scale 1 rather than dividing by zero — the corpus asserts the number, because a NaN transform is an invisible animation nobody can debug. Numbers are asserted to 1e-6; PIXELS are the vendor renderer's and are not pinned anywhere in this corpus. Function: riveFit(fit, alignment, cw, ch, bw, bh) on all three.",
